{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_9004f404fe0a4f6f8e264400","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Worklog: third-party plugin discovery contribution seam\n2\t\n3\t## Run Metadata\n4\t\n5\t| Field          | Value                                           |\n6\t| -------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n7\t| Run ID         | `fix-plugin-discovery-contribution-seam--0.0.7` |\n8\t| Branch         | `fix/plugin-discovery-contribution-seam`        |\n9\t| Base           | `bd9d463b4480847dcd6f76efe5bc1e53bb926bec`      |\n10\t| Archetype      | `4 — Public DSL / Builder`                      |\n11\t| Scope overlays | none                                            |\n12\t| Phase          | S3 implementation complete; fresh IMPL-EVAL pending |\n13\t\n14\tThe leaf brief explicitly limits S1 output to `research.md`, `plan.md`, and `worklog.md`; the\n15\tsupervisor owns run identity, routing, and PLAN-EVAL disposition. No implementation may begin from\n16\tthis session.\n17\t\n18\t## Design\n19\t\n20\t### Public Surface\n21\t\n22\t- `ContributionBuilderPattern` — readonly public `callee -> axis` descriptor on\n23\t  `@netscript/plugin/sdk`.\n24\t- `AstExtractorOptions` — readonly `additionalBuilders` configuration.\n25\t- `new AstExtractor(options?)` — optional per-instance extension while preserving the no-arg path.\n26\t- `startWalker(root, options?)` — forwards extractor options while preserving `startWalker(root)`.\n27\t\n28\t### Caller-Facing Shape\n29\t\n30\t```ts\n31\tconst extractor = new AstExtractor({\n32\t  additionalBuilders: [\n33\t    { callee: 'defineChannelSync', axis: 'channel-syncs' },\n34\t  ],\n35\t});\n36\t\n37\tconst contributions = await extractor.extract(files);\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\tThe 80-percent existing path remains `new AstExtractor()` or `startWalker(root)`.\n41\t\n42\t### Domain Vocabulary\n43\t\n44\t- **Contribution builder pattern** — a validated source-level factory identifier paired with the\n45\t  contribution axis emitted for direct exported calls.\n46\t- **Official defaults** — the immutable `defineJob/jobs`, `defineSaga/sagas`, and\n47\t  `defineWebhook/triggers` mappings.\n48\t- **Additional builders** — caller-owned patterns appended for one extractor instance.\n49\t- **Extracted contribution** — existing `{ file, symbol, axis }` output; unchanged.\n50\t\n51\t### Ports\n52\t\n53\t- `ExtractorPort` remains the consumed abstraction and does not change shape.\n54\t- `WalkerPort`/`WalkedFile` remain unchanged; the walker discovers text and must not learn factory\n55\t  semantics.\n56\t- `EmitterPort` remains unchanged; it consumes arbitrary axis strings already.\n57\t- No new port is justified.\n58\t\n59\t### Constants\n60\t\n61\t- Private `DEFAULT_CONTRIBUTION_BUILDERS` — exactly the existing three official mappings.\n62\t- Private TypeScript identifier validation expression — protects regex construction.\n63\t- No global mutable registry constant/state.\n64\t\n65\t### Validation Rules\n66\t\n67\t- `callee` must be a TypeScript identifier accepted by the extractor's direct-call grammar.\n68\t- `axis` must be non-blank; emitter normalization remains unchanged.\n69\t- Duplicate callees, including official collisions, throw a clear `TypeError`.\n70\t- Constructor snapshots caller input.\n71\t\n72\t### Commit Slices\n73\t\n74\t|  # | Slice                                                                                                         | Gate                                                                       | Files                                                                |\n75\t| -: | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n76\t|  1 | Introduce descriptor/options contracts, configure `AstExtractor`, and prove synthetic plus official behavior. | focused structured test; scoped check/lint/fmt; quality scan               | `extractor-port.ts`, `ast-extractor.ts`, `walker-ports_test.ts`      |\n77\t|  2 | Forward options through `startWalker`, export/document the SDK surface, and verify package publish contracts. | focused structured test; `deno doc`; doc/JSR non-increase; publish dry-run | `start-walker.ts`, `sdk/mod.ts`, `README.md`, focused test if needed |\n78\t\n79\t### Deferred Scope\n80\t\n81\t- CLI descriptor transport — separately owned `packages/cli` integration.\n82\t- Manifest declaration/resolution — not implied by the current pipeline.\n83\t- Compiler AST/symbol binding — existing `PLG-WALKER-AST` debt.\n84\t- MCP corpus regeneration — report to the supervisor because `packages/mcp` is outside ceiling.\n85\t- Existing unrelated doctrine/JSR/doc-lint debt — exact non-increase only.\n86\t\n87\t### Contributor Path\n88\t\n89\tA third-party author or host tooling imports `AstExtractor` from `@netscript/plugin/sdk`, supplies\n90\tone additional `{ callee, axis }` pattern at composition, and passes that extractor to the existing\n91\tpipeline (or uses the option-forwarding preset). Adding a factory does not require editing\n92\t`packages/plugin` defaults. Automatic CLI pickup remains a separately coordinated consumer step.\n93\t\n94\t## Progress Log\n95\t\n96\t| Time (UTC) | Slice | Step             | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n97\t| ---------- | ----- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n98\t| 2026-08-31 | S1    | Bootstrap        | Read harness activation/run-loop, Archetype 4, gate matrix, Pla