n green                                 |\n137\t| Full export doc-lint     | FAIL (pre-existing)     | 15 private refs; 0 missing JSDoc; 0 other                                  | <=15; missing/other 0; no owned-file finding |\n138\t| JSR package audit        | FAIL (pre-existing)     | 4 FAIL, 2 WARN, 1 INFO; dry-run OK                                         | exact non-increase; no owned-file finding    |\n139\t| Package publish dry-run  | PASS with warnings      | exactly 2 unanalyzable dynamic imports at existing locations               | no new warning/count                         |\n140\t| Code-quality scan        | PASS                    | 0 findings, 0 allowances                                                   | remain green                                 |\n141\t| Scoped doctrine          | PASS exit with findings | 0 FAIL, 3 WARN, 1 INFO                                                     | exact non-increase                           |\n142\t| Lock hygiene after gates | PASS                    | SHA-256 `edfa0c24b70e0d830acce68aad6f5da42b66a88527aef4b80f3f82d989d1820c` | byte-identical                               |\n143\t\n144\t### Fitness Gate Coverage\n145\t\n146\tArchetype-4 F-1 through F-12 plus F-14 through F-19 are represented by the scoped wrappers, quality\n147\tscan, doctrine scan, JSR audit, doc-lint, publish dry-run, and manual design review. Existing debt\n148\tremains explicit; no green wrapper is treated as proof that the pre-existing findings vanished.\n149\t\n150\t### Runtime and Consumer Gates\n151\t\n152\t- Runtime/browser/scaffold/E2E/Aspire/Docker: N/A and forbidden in S1.\n153\t- Focused unit proof: NOT RUN in S1 due the static-only constraint; S2 final result is 9 passed / 0\n154\t  failed through the structured test wrapper.\n155\t- CLI consumers: inspected statically; both remain protected by no-arg compatibility, but automatic\n156\t  third-party descriptor transport is not claimed.\n157\t- MCP corpus: impact confirmed statically; freshness check/regeneration not run because it is\n158\t  cross-package and outside the ceiling. The stale generated path and owner handoff are recorded in\n159\t  `drift.md`; the corpus did not move.\n160\t\n161\t### S2 Slice Evidence\n162\t\n163\t| Slice | State | Command | Result |\n164\t| ----- | ----- | ------- | ------ |\n165\t| S2.1 | RED compile | `deno run --allow-read --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-check.ts --root packages/plugin --ext ts,tsx` | PASS: 153 files, 2 batches, 0 findings |\n166\t| S2.1 | RED behavior | `deno run --allow-read --allow-write --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-test.ts -- --allow-all packages/plugin/tests/sdk/walker-ports_test.ts` | expected FAIL: 5 passed, 2 failed, 7 total, 2 unique failures |\n167\t| S2.1 | GREEN behavior | same focused structured test command | PASS: 7 passed, 0 failed |\n168\t| S2.1 | GREEN check | same scoped check command | PASS: 153 files, 2 batches, 0 findings |\n169\t| S2.1 | GREEN lint | `deno run --allow-read --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-lint.ts --root packages/plugin --ext ts,tsx` | PASS: 153 processed, 0 dropped/refused/findings |\n170\t| S2.1 | GREEN format | `deno run --allow-read --allow-run .llm/tools/run-deno-fmt.ts --root packages/plugin --ext ts,tsx` | PASS: 153 processed, 0 findings |\n171\t| S2.1 | GREEN quality | `deno run --allow-read .llm/tools/quality/scan-code-quality.ts --root packages/plugin --max-allow 0` | PASS: 0 findings, 0 allowances |\n172\t| S2.2 | RED compile | same scoped check command | PASS: 153 files, 2 batches, 0 findings |\n173\t| S2.2 | RED behavior | same focused structured test command | expected FAIL: 7 passed, 1 failed, 8 total, 1 unique failure |\n174\t| S2.2 | GREEN behavior | same focused structured test command | PASS: 9 passed, 0 failed |\n175\t| S2.2 | Public surface | `deno doc --filter <symbol> packages/plugin/src/sdk/mod.ts` for both new types, `AstExtractor`, and `startWalker` | PASS: documented exported types and explicit optional parameters rendered |\n176\t\n177\t### S2 Final Gate Contracts\n178\t\n179\t| Gate | Final result | Baseline contract |\n180\t| ---- | ------------ | ----------------- |\n181\t| Scoped check | PASS: 153 files, 2 batches, 0 findings | green preserved |\n182\t| Scoped lint | PASS: 153 processed, 0 dropped/refused/findings | green preserved |\n183\t| Scoped format | PASS: 153 processed, 0 findings | green preserved |\n184\t| Code-quality scan | PASS: 0 findings, 0 allowances | green preserved |\n185\t| Full export doc-lint | expected exit 1: 15 private refs, 0 missing JSDoc, 0 other; `./sdk` has 0 | exact non-increase (15/0/0) |\n186\t| JSR package audit | expected exit 1: 4 FAIL, 2 WARN, 1 INFO; no owned-file finding | exact non-increase (4/2/1) |\n187\t| Package publish dry-run | PASS; same two unanalyzable dynamic imports at `generated-project-registry.ts:69` and `manifest-resolver.ts:33` | warning count/locations unchanged |\n188\t| Scoped doctrine | exit 0: 0 FAIL, 2 WARN, 1 INFO | improved from 0/3/1; no new finding |\n189\t| Lock hygiene | SHA-256 `edfa0c24b70e0d830acce68aad6f5da42b66a88527aef4b80f3f82d989d1820c` | byte-identical |\n190\t\n191\t## Handoff Notes\n192\t\n193\t1. PLAN-EVAL should challenge whether package-level extractor configuration satisfies the intended\n194\t   acceptance or whether automatic CLI transport is required; if the latter, rescope before S2.\n195\t2. Inspect the locked ceiling before implementation. Any manifest, CLI, MCP, generated-asset, or\n196\t   lock edit is a stop condition.\n197\t3. The decisive review point is the synthetic `defineChannelSync` test without a fourth default\n198\t   table row, paired with unchanged official-factory behavior.\n199\t4. Preserve the exact baseline reds; unrelated cleanup would obscure the narrow change.\n200\t5. Coordinate the known MCP corpus stale result with its owner rather than regenerating it here.\n201\t\n202\t## 2026-09-01 — S3 implementation\n203\t\n204\t### Outcome\n205\t\n206\t- The generic plugin SDK no longer contains any official factory-to-axis mapping. Workers, sagas,\n207\t  and triggers each emit `NETSCRIPT_CONTRIBUTION_BUILDERS` from the control-plane module their\n208\t  adapter already owns.\n209\t- `AstExtractor` discovers those declarations from its existing `WalkedFile` input, merges them with\n210\t  its immutable per-instance `additionalBuilders`, and rejects malformed or duplicate callees.\n211\t- A recognizable direct contribution-factory call imported from a plugin core now throws a\n212\t  remedy-bearing `TypeError` when no walked declaration or `additionalBuilders` entry owns it. A\n213\t  walk with no such call remains quietly empty.\n214\t- The quality scanner now emits `plugin-discovery-core-coupling` when host/core source under\n215\t  `packages/**` contains a literal `{ callee, axis }` mapping or compares/predicates a `callee` or\n216\t  `axis` against a literal. Plugin engine packages (`packages/plugin-*-core/**`) and connector-owned\n217\t  declarations under `plugins/**` remain allowed.\n218\t- The canonical MCP corpus was regenerated. This incidentally clears the deterministic staleness\n219\t  tracked by #1873; this slice makes no claim about adding that check to CI.\n220\t\n221\t### Migration boundary\n222\t\n223\tProjects scaffolded before S3 do not yet have plugin-owned discovery declarations. Before using\n224\tno-argument discovery they must re-run plugin sync/update so the official control-plane modules are\n225\tregenerated. Passing `additionalBuilders` is the explicit compatibility path. Keeping the old core\n226\ttable as a fallback was rejected because it would make the responsibility move cosmetic.\n227\t\n228\t### RED / GREEN evidence\n229\t\n230\t| Slice | State | Commit | Command and result |\n231\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n232\t| S3.1 declaration transport | RED | `aea929b054fdbb0011a8a08ea1618314ba4e111a` | Structured checks passed for 153 package files and 265 plugin files; focused structured tests exited 1 wit