{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788284697-lNPzYws2B2Lrf8VQy4bF","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key facts established:\n\n1. **Test files are excluded** (`isScannable` returns false for `_test.ts`) — so `walker-ports_test.ts` with its `{ callee: 'defineJob', axis: 'jobs' }` fixtures is not scanned. Production-only, per D5. ✓\n2. **Allowances are inline `// quality-allow: #<issue> — <reason>` markers**, not a numeric budget. `--max-allow 7` only caps the *count of allowances* (so people can't add unlimited allowances). A planted violation produces a *finding*, which makes `ok=false` → exit 1 regardless of max-allow. ✓ So the supervisor's exit-1 probe claim is structurally sound, and I still need to reproduce it.\n3. Findings from `pluginDiscoveryCoreCoupling` are pushed into `findings` — wait, I need to check how they interact with the per-line `ruleFor` loop. Looking at the diff: `findings.push(...pluginDiscoveryCoreCoupling(unit.lines.join('\\n'), normalized));` happens per unit — these are pushed directly into findings, NOT through the per-line loop. So an inline `quality-allow:` comment on a coupling line would NOT suppress it (the allowance marker logic works on `ruleFor(line...)`, and if `ruleFor` returns nothing but the structural rule fired, the allowance would be... hmm, interesting: a `quality-allow` marker on a line where `ruleFor` is clean and no public/discarded finding → `continue` (dead weight, not counted). So the structural rule cannot be suppressed by inline allowances — good for guard strength. But note: that also means the finding lines counted twice? No — they're separate pushes; structural findings are added once per unit.\n\nWait, actually there's a subtlety: `pluginDiscoveryCoreCoupling` gets `unit.lines.join('\\n')` — the unit source. For markdown docs-site files, units are code fences; for TS files the whole file. OK.\n\nAnother subtlety: `isHostCoreSource` checks `normalized.startsWith('packages/')`. The scanner runs from repo root with `--root packages`, and `unit.sourcePath` is `relative(cwd, file)` → `packages/plugin/src/...`. ✓. But when CI runs `--changed-file` mode with paths like `packages/...`, still fine.\n\nNow let me run the E2 probe experiments. I'll create probe files, run the scanner, capture output, delete probes.\n\nProbe plan (as listed): create `packages/plugin/src/sdk/discovery/__eval_probe.ts` with branch + table + switch + reversed comparison + startsWith, using a non-today callee `defineExample` and non-today axis `examples`.\n\nWait — one probe file can't have everything because line attribution matters, but for exit-code purposes one file with multiple forms is fine; I'll also do separate minimal files per form to attribute precisely. Let me be efficient: create 3 probe files in packages/plugin/src/sdk/discovery/: `__probe_branch.ts`, `__probe_table.ts`, `__probe_misc.ts` (switch + reversed + startsWith + escape attempts). And one in plugins/sagas/src/adapter/ and one in packages/plugin-workers-core/src/ for the exclusion checks.\n\nThen run: `deno run --allow-read .llm/tools/quality/scan-code-quality.ts --root packages --root plugins` (no --max-allow needed; I only care about findings + exit). Actually to mirror quality:scan, add the docs/site root too — not needed for probe attribution. I'll run with `--root packages` first, then `--root plugins`.\n\nNote the scanner needs `--allow-net=api.github.com --allow-env=GITHUB_TOKEN,GH_TOKEN` per the task definition (probably for validating allowance issue references via GitHub API — allowanceFailures need issue refs; my probes have no allowances so no net needed... but the code may still call out for validating allowances elsewhere in the tree; the 7 pre-existing allowances in the repo would need validation. To be safe use the same flags as the task).\n\nThen delete probes and re-run to confirm exit 0 (clean baseline).\n\nLet me write the probe files now. Careful to make them realistic TS that compiles (scanner doesn't compile, but no matter).\n\nAlso for E2's \"would it fire on a callee that is not one of today's three\" — `defineExample`/`examples` covers that.\n\nLet me also verify the RED test file for the guard (scan-code-quality_test.ts +28) to see what fixtures it plants.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"87a74253-d0e6-4f02-8f0d-3fe28a0e7b40","uuid":"8a4af72d-93d1-4daf-9443-43dd7b6c75fa","timestamp":"2026-09-01T17:45:25.494Z","request_id":"gen-1788284697-lNPzYws2B2Lrf8VQy4bF"}
