earlier S2 head independently\\nreproduced both RED commits and correctly passed the immutable `additionalBuilders` seam, its\\nsynthetic `defineChannelSync → channel-syncs` registry emission, malformed/duplicate handling, and\\nthe then-current no-argument compatibility oracle. It did not evaluate the later S3 responsibility\\nmove or architectural guard.\\n\\n## Correction — acceptance was overstated; boxes 2 and 5 are NOT satisfied\\n\\nA merge audit found this PR's acceptance false, and I verified it before accepting the finding:\\n\\n- **Box 2 is unimplemented.** `packages/plugin/src/sdk/discovery/ast-extractor.ts:10-14` still hardcodes\\n  `defineSaga → sagas` and `defineWebhook → triggers` inside `DEFAULT_CONTRIBUTION_BUILDERS` — in\\n  **plugin core**. Box 2 requires those axes to be **declared by `plugins/sagas` and\\n  `plugins/triggers`**, which is the opposite of what shipped. The extension seam this PR adds is real\\n  and works for *third-party* factories; it does not move the official ones out of core.\\n- **Box 5 is unimplemented.** No `arch:check` rule or guard test fails when a core package gains a\\n  plugin-specific branch. My earlier evidence cited the duplicate-callee throw, which prevents a\\n  duplicate row — a different thing entirely.\\n- **`check:mcp-export-corpus` regresses** on this branch (generator error), attributable to the new\\n  exports.\\n- The prior IMPL-EVAL is **stale**: `packages/plugin/README.md` changed after it ran.\\n\\nI wrote that acceptance evidence and mirrored it. That was my error, not the evaluator's — the\\nIMPL-EVAL judged the seam it was asked to judge and judged it correctly; I then over-claimed two boxes\\nit never covered. Boxes 2 and 5 are un-ticked on the issue with the same explanation recorded there,\\nthe PR is back to `status:impl`, and `impl-eval:skip` is removed so no stale attribution stands.\\n\\n**Remaining work before this is re-offered:** implement the full accepted scope (move the official\\naxis declarations to their owning plugins; add the doctrine/guard check), regenerate the export-surface\\ncorpus, then a fresh exact-head delta IMPL-EVAL and current CI.\\n\\n`.llm/runs` artifacts are preserved throughout — under owner policy their presence is valid and they\\nare never stripped.\\n\\n## S3 implementation — boxes 2 and 5 are now genuinely implemented\\n\\nThe correction above remains the historical record of the bad acceptance claim. The missing scope is\\nnow present in code:\\n\\n- **Box 2:** `DEFAULT_CONTRIBUTION_BUILDERS` was removed. Workers, sagas, and triggers emit their\\n  mappings from their own adapters; a synthetic third-party declaration is discovered without\\n  constructor options or a core edit. No-argument consumers receive official mappings through walked\\n  plugin control-plane modules, not through a core fallback.\\n- **Box 5:** `plugin-discovery-core-coupling` is part of the scanner used by\\n  `quality:gate`. Its deliberately planted `defineExample` fixture produces one finding for a\\n  literal mapping table and one for a core branch, while identical connector-owned code is allowed.\\n- **Silent migration failure:** an unmatched recognizable factory call now throws with the callee and\\n  regeneration/`additionalBuilders` remedy; an actually empty walk stays quiet.\\n- **Corpus:** canonical regeneration makes `deno task check:mcp-export-corpus` exit 0. This\\n  incidentally clears the deterministic staleness tracked by #1873; it does **not** implement or claim\\n  #1873's separate CI-gating work.\\n\\nRED/GREEN commits:\\n\\n- declaration transport: RED `aea929b05` (30 pass / 6 fail), GREEN `9cb326dae` (36/36);\\n- architectural guard: RED `63c9dac34` (28 pass / 1 fail), GREEN `026032d5d` (29/29);\\n- canonical corpus: `67c718a4c`, check exit 0.\\n\\nExact-head static gates are green: `quality:gate`, `arch:check`, package check (153 files), package\\ntests (92/92), official-plugin checks (265 files), focused plugin tests (23/23), scanner tests\\n(29/29), and corpus freshness. Pre-existing package reds did not increase: doc-lint remains 15\\nprivate refs / 0 missing JSDoc / 0 other; JSR audit remains 4 FAIL / 2 WARN / 1 INFO; publish dry-run\\nretains exactly its two known dynamic-import warnings.\\n\\n## Definition of Done\\n\\n- [x] A third-party factory is discovered end to end without editing core defaults, proven by a synthetic fixture and a real temp-dir registry emission.\\n- [x] The official factories are discovered for no-arg consumers through plugin-owned declarations, with no core fallback.\\n- [x] Malformed, duplicate, and unmatched contribution factories fail loudly rather than being silently dropped.\\n- [x] `packages/config` path-constants question decided and recorded (no manifest schema or config-path change).\\n- [x] `defineJob`, `defineSaga`, and `defineWebhook` axes are declared by their owning plugins, not by plugin core.\\n- [x] A doctrine guard fails when host/core gains a literal plugin-specific factory mapping or branch.\\n- [x] `check:mcp-export-corpus` is green at the exact head.\\n- [ ] Fresh exact-head delta IMPL-EVAL passes.\\n- [ ] Exact-head CI is green and review threads are zero.\\n\\n## Supervisor verification at the integrated head `2398b9fe5`\\n\\nMeasured independently of the implementation session.\\n\\n### The generated corpus conflicted with #1862 and was resolved through its generator\\n\\nMerging `origin/main` `82a2527e2` conflicted on\\n`packages/mcp/src/infrastructure/export-surfaces/export-surface-corpus.generated.ts`, because #1862\\nregenerated the same carrier on `main` in parallel. Resolved by **regenerating**, never by picking a\\nside; `check:mcp-export-corpus` then exits 0, and symbol count moves `7782` → `7784` — this branch's\\nown new exports rather than a stale carry.\\n\\nThis makes the corpus fresh here and on `main`. It does **not** close #1873, whose remaining half is\\nthat `check:mcp-export-corpus` runs in **no** workflow and can drift again silently. Not claimed.\\n\\n### The box-5 guard is proven non-vacuous, not merely green\\n\\nA green `quality:gate` is not evidence the new rule works — it could be green because the rule never\\nfires. Tested by planting a violation in a core package:\\n\\n```ts\\n// packages/plugin/src/sdk/discovery/__planted_probe.ts\\nexport function axisFor(callee: string): string | undefined {\\n  if (callee === 'defineExample') return 'examples';\\n  return undefined;\\n}\\n```\\n\\n| State | `quality:scan` |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| planted violation present | **exit 1** — `plugin-discovery-core-coupling` at `__planted_probe.ts:3`, offending line quoted |\\n| probe removed | **exit 0** |\\n\\n`defineExample` is deliberately **not** one of today's three callees, so the rule is generic and\\ncannot degrade into a three-name snapshot. Probe deleted; worktree clean.\\n\\n### The clean break does not reintroduce the silent failure this issue was filed about\\n\\nSupervisor review made this mandatory before implementation. Deleting the core defaults means a\\nproject generated before this change has real factory call sites and no declaration — which would\\nextract **zero contributions silently**, i.e. the exact defect #1093 describes, moved to a new\\ntrigger. `ast-extractor.ts:105-122` now throws when a file imports a contribution factory from\\nplugin core **and** has export call sites for it but no declaration supplies an axis:\\n\\n```\\nContribution factory \\\"\\u003ccallee\\u003e\\\" has no declared axis; run plugin sync/update or pass it through additionalBuilders\\n```\\n\\nand stays quiet when there are no call sites — the boundary that was specified.\\n\\n### Gates\\n\\n| Gate | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `deno task quality:gate` | **exit 0** |\\n| `deno task arch:check` | **exit 0** |\\n| `run-deno-test.ts` on `packages/plugin` | **92 passed / 0 failed** |\\n| `run-deno-check.ts --root packages/plugin --ext ts` | 153 files, 2 batches, **0 diagnostics** |\\n| `deno task check:mcp-export-corpus` | **exit 0** |\\n| `deno.lock` | blob **byte-identical** to `origin/main` `82a2527e2` |\\n\\nRemaining before this is offered for merge: a fresh separate-session exact-head IMPL-EVAL, and green\\nexact-head CI. Neither is claimed here.\\n\\n## Acceptance evidence (issue #1093)\\n\\n```acceptance-evidence\\nissue: 1093\\nentries:\\n  - box-index: 1\\n    evidence: \\\"AstExtractor accepts immutable per-instance AstExtractorOptions.additionalBuilders and startWalker forwards them, so a third-party factory participates without a core edit.\\\"\\n  - box-index: 2\\n    evidence: \\\"DEFAULT_CONTRIBUTION_BUILDERS is removed. Workers, sagas, and triggers each emit NETSCRIPT_CONTRIBUTION_BUILDERS from their owned control-plane adapter, and no-arg extraction reads those walked declarations with no host-side plugin import or core fallback.\\\"\\n  - box-index: 3\\n    evidence: \\\"A synthetic defineChannelSync -\\u003e channel-syncs declaration is discovered without editing core defaults or passing constructor options; the earlier real-temp-dir additionalBuilders registry proof also remains.\\\"\\n  - box-index: 4\\n    evidence: \\\"No manifest schema, packages/config path constant, or new cross-package dependency was needed. The authorized canonical MCP corpus regeneration is isolated to its generated file.\\\"\\n  - box-index: 5\\n    evidence: \\\"The quality scanner emits plugin-discovery-core-coupling for an arbitrary defineExample mapping table and branch in host core, while allowing the identical plugin-owned fixture. quality:gate exits nonzero on such findings; encoded strings, computed keys, and cross-file aliases are stated limits.\\\"\\n```\\n\\n\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"fix(plugin-core): let third-party plugin factories participate in discovery\"}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
